namespace jo

//[ The contract for the program entry point
  !
  ! The compiler locates the entry point by looking for a top-level function
  ! named `main` that takes no parameters, and checks it against this
  ! signature. It is an error if no such function exists. If several do, name
  ! the entry point explicitly by passing `--link jo.main=app.main` to the
  ! compiler.
  !
  ! The `receives` clause lists the capabilities the runtime makes available to
  ! the entry point. It is not a requirement: a `main` that uses only some of
  ! them — or none at all — still conforms. Nor is it an upper bound: a build
  ! may inject further context parameters with `--provide`, and a `main` that
  ! receives a provided parameter still conforms. See the Entry Point section
  ! of the language documentation.
  !
  ! There is no standard input capability. A program that reads input obtains it
  ! from a backend-specific API, such as `py.input`, and passes it on as its own
  ! context parameter.
  !
  ! The `pass` body is only a placeholder, so that this declaration is a
  ! well-formed deferred function; the program supplies the real entry point.
//]
defer def main: Unit receives IO.stdout, IO.stderr, IO.args = pass
